description:
FILED s520b (Opus, 2026-10-18) while fixing #3365 (the single-element `local($$r) = LIST`).

  our ($g, $y) = (1, 0); my $r = "g";
  { local($$r, $y) = (7, 8); print "g=$g y=$y\n"; }
  print "g=$g y=$y\n";
perl 5.40.3: g=7 y=8 / g=1 y=0.   fd04c048 and s520b: `PCL: statement dropped ... Parser2 TODO: unsupported `local` target: $$r` and the run dies at that statement (LOUD, not silent).

Where: Pl/Parser.pm _process_local_declaration's @items path (`_local_list_items` / `_local_target_item`) has no item kind for a Cast-led scalar deref; the single-element spelling goes through the deref branch (p-local-deref-scalar) since s519a's pre-unwrap, with LIST context restored by #3365.  Fix shape: a `deref` item kind in the list path reusing the deref branch's place (Pl::ExprToCL::_cast_form) and p-local-deref-scalar's save/restore.  Low priority: no corpus file has the shape (corpus-diff), perl-tests/local.t's deref rows are single-element.
